<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Missolonghi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mesolongi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Missolonghi, or Mesolongi, is a town on a lagoon at the mouth of the Gulf of Patras in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence">Greek War of Independence</a> it was the centre of the revolution in western Greece and withstood several sieges, until its defenders broke out in April 1826 and the town fell to Ottoman and Egyptian forces. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lord-byron">Lord Byron</a> died there in 1824.</p></div>
